        <body>
            <div xml:id="d190-a2-a1">

                <pb facs="0361" n="289" xml:id="pg289"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Meany’s Arrest</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Dublin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-08-12"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi>
                        12</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>It now appears that Stephen J. Meany was arrested on Thursday night at Brennan’s
                    Hotel, Ennis, under a warrant of the lord lieutenant, charging him with being a
                    dangerous character. He was detained all night at the police barracks and
                    discharged in the morning on giving bail for good behavior for six months. His
                    trunks were searched but nothing of a treasonable character was found in
                    them.</p>
            </div>
